<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of second round first</p>
<p>leg matches in African club soccer competitions on Sunday:</p>
<p>Champions' Cup:</p>
<p>In Harare: Caps United (Zimbabwe) 1 Orlando Pirates (South</p>
<p>Africa) 2 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Caps United - Stewart Murisa 10</p>
<p>Orlando Pirates - Gerald Stober 49, Dumisani Mpofu 79 (own</p>
<p>goal)</p>
<p>Attendance: 25,000</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Tunis: Club africain (Tunisia) 6 Saint-Pierroise</p>
<p>(Reunion) 1 (halftime 5-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>C Africain - Issam Abdelhak 12, Lantam Wadja 18, 33, 35,</p>
<p>Faouzi Rouissi 44, Belhassen Aloui 84</p>
<p>Saint-Pierroise - Bernard Lacollay 49 pen</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Casablanca: Raja Casablanca (Morocco) 3 Mbilinga (Gabon)</p>
<p>0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Moustaoudaa Mustapha 20, 55, Jinani Abdelkrim 22</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
<p>	  Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Bouake, Ivory Coast: Africa Sports (Ivory Coast) 1</p>
<p>Primiero Agosto (Angola) 1 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Africa Sports - Patrick Mancha 14</p>
<p>Primiero Agosto - Bixente Francisco 89</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
<p>Cup Winners Cup</p>
<p>In Accra: Hearts of Oak (Ghana) 2 Etoile Sahel (Tunisia) 2</p>
<p>(halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Hearts of Oak - Desmond Amoah 21 Owusu Afriyie 80</p>
<p>Etoile Sahel - Zoubeir Beya 9 Ismael Pereira 91 injury time</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>In Bouake, Ivory Coast: SO Armee (Ivory Coast) v Dragons</p>
<p>(Zaire). Match postponed until Monday following Dragons' late</p>
<p>arrival.</p>
<p>CAF Cup</p>
<p>In Kumasi: Asante Kotoko (Ghana) 1 USM Ein Beida (Algeria) 1</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Asante Kotoko - Prince Adu Poku 31</p>
<p>USM Ein Beida - Segir 77</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Douala: Unisport Bafang (Cameroon) 1 Ferroviario Maputo</p>
<p>(Mozambique) 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Tokene Bertin 74</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>CAF Cup</p>
<p>In Ouagadougou: USFA (Burkina Faso) 1 Esperance (Tunisia) 1</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>USFA - Abdoulaye Traore 23</p>
<p>Esperance - Ben Ahmed Faycal 48</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
